till charged. So, the agent informed the customer, "We sincerely apologize for the inconvenience caused and the delay in our response. We appreciate your patience, and we are writing to you regarding the concern which you have raised with us. We would like to inform you that your loan account reflects a total of 30 EPI updated as of Dec'25. Your regular EPI amount is INR 4,799.65. However, the EPI for Dec'25 is showing as INR 5,539.09, which is higher than the standard amount. This difference of INR 739.44 is due to an adjustment related to broken period interest. Broken period interest refers to the interest charged for the period between the loan disbursement date and the actual EPI cycle start date. This adjustment is typically reflected in one of the early EPI or during a reconciliation period, as in your case. We assure you that this adjustment has been made in accordance with your loan amortization schedule. Additionally, we wish to inform you that your EPI for the month of Dec'25 was returned due to a bounce. Consequently, bounce charges will be levied by both DMI and the registered bank.'</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>100</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>100</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>DMI</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>-</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>Retail Email & Tickets</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>-</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>-</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>01-03-26 11:47:55</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>Jan'26</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'></td><td style='border:1px solid black;'></td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>-</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>Pass</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>10</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>10</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'></td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>0</td><td style='border:1px solid black;'></td><td style='border:1px solid black;'>N/A</td><td style='border:1px solid black